description:
## Defect

`re-frame.story.determinism/->artifact` turns a normalized variant plan into a replayable run artifact. It keeps only four things:
- `[:world :setup]` ⧺ `:script`;
- `[:world :frame :fx-overrides]`;
- `[:world :network]`;
- a `:source`.

Everything else in the plan's world that shapes the variant's run is dropped. The two that bite are:
- the `:fx-override` decorators, i.e. every `[:rf.story/force-fx-stub …]`. The frames runtime installs these at frame creation, and they never appear in `[:world :frame :fx-overrides]`.
- `[:world :db-seed]`.

Frame-setup decorators and loaders are dropped too.

Three consumers replay that lossy artifact instead of the variant's own world:
- the determinism gate (`assert-deterministic`), given `(story/variant-plan id)`;
- golden capture and compare given a plan (`capture-golden`, `compare-golden`, `golden-match?`);
- any caller of `->artifact`.

A variant that stubs an effect therefore has the REAL effect handler invoked by the gate. A seeded variant replays from an empty app-db. The gate or the golden then reports on a run the variant never makes.

## Where

All cites are at `034d0c8fc8`.
- `tools/story/src/re_frame/story/determinism.cljc:66-114` is `->artifact`. The plan branch at `:98-110` builds `{:setup … :script … :fx-decisions (get-in target [:world :frame :fx-overrides] {}) :source …}` plus `:network`. `[:world :decorators]` and `[:world :db-seed]` are never read.
- `determinism.cljc:217-284` is `assert-deterministic`, which calls `(->artifact plan-or-artifact)` at `:252`.
- `tools/story/src/re_frame/story/golden.cljc:215` is `->run-result`. A plan target becomes `(replay-run-artifact (->artifact target) opts)`, and `capture-golden`, `compare-golden` and `golden-match?` all go through it.
- `tools/story/src/re_frame/story/artifact.cljc:402-483` is `replay-run-artifact`. The fresh frame gets no decorator stubs and no seed.
- Public entry points:
  - `re-frame.story/assert-deterministic` (`story.cljc:1210`);
  - `capture-golden` (`:1324`);
  - `golden-match?` (`:1336`);
  - `compare-golden` (`:1347`);
  - each taking `(story/variant-plan id)`.
- Contract:
  - `tools/story/spec/017-Testing-Story.md:3493-3494`: the gate answers "does this plan / artifact produce the same run every time?";
  - `:3510-3512` names only the setup/script and fx-overrides fold;
  - spec 005 §force-fx-stub, where the stub is "per-frame and per-variant", i.e. a property of the variant's world.

## Failure scenario

Register an fx `:probe.fx/http` that counts its calls and throws. Register `:probe/load`, which emits it. Then:
- `(story/reg-variant :story.probe/stubbed {:decorators [[:rf.story/force-fx-stub :probe.fx/http {:status 200}]] :script [[:dispatch [:probe/load]]]})`:
  - `run-variant` returns `:pass` with 0 real calls;
  - `(story/assert-deterministic (story/variant-plan :story.probe/stubbed))` makes 2 REAL calls to the stubbed handler, sees both replays `:fail`, and returns `:non-deterministic`;
  - `(story/capture-golden (story/variant-plan :story.probe/stubbed))` freezes a golden whose run is `:fail` and makes 1 real call.
- `(story/reg-variant :story.probe/seeded {:db-seed {:count 10} :script [[:dispatch [:probe/inc]]]})`:
  - `run-variant` returns `:pass` with app-db `{:count 11}`;
  - replaying `(->artifact (story/variant-plan :story.probe/seeded))` ends at `{:count 1}`.

In practice, a stubbed HTTP or analytics call really fires from a CI determinism or golden job, and a seeded variant's golden freezes the unseeded run.

## Evidence

All of this was EXECUTED: a one-shot JVM script through `clojure.main`, on the `tools/story` `:test` classpath, in the frozen tree (scratch `probe1.clj` / `probe1.out`, section B).
- The variant itself:
  - B0 `run-variant` stubbed gives `[:pass :real-fx-calls 0]`;
  - B5 `run-variant` seeded gives `[:pass {… :count 11}]`.
- The compiled plan:
  - B1 `[:world :frame :fx-overrides]` is `nil`;
  - B1 `[:world :decorators]` is `[[:rf.story/force-fx-stub :probe.fx/http {:status 200}]]`;
  - B6 `[:world :db-seed]` is `{:count 10}`;
  - B2 `->artifact` gives `{:event-program [[:dispatch [:probe/load]]], :fx-decisions {}}`.
- The replays:
  - B3 `assert-deterministic` gives `[:non-deterministic [:fail :fail] :real-fx-calls 2]`;
  - B4 `capture-golden` gives `[:fail … :real-fx-calls 1]`;
  - B7 the seeded replay app-db is `{:count 1}`.

The B3 `:non-deterministic` verdict (rather than a stable `:fail`) is compounded by a separate defect filed alongside this one: canonicalization does not strip `:error-trace`. The load-bearing facts here are the real-fx calls and the unseeded app-db.

No tracker duplicate. The nearest are rf2-siyxz (the promotion snippet dropped `:network`/`:fx-overrides`, closed) and rf2-rky08 / rf2-cml0h (promotion lost run inputs, closed); neither touches `->artifact`'s world fold.

## Smallest fix

Make the plan to artifact fold carry the run-shaping world the runtime applies:
- lower the plan's `:fx-override` decorators into `:fx-decisions`, and make sure the stub fx they point at is registered for the replay frame. Today `frames/ensure-stub-event!` registers it only during variant frame setup;
- carry `[:world :db-seed]` in a new artifact slot that `replay-run-artifact` seeds before the program;
- fold frame-setup decorator `:init` events into the program's setup prefix.

The alternative, if a full fold is judged too wide, is for `->artifact` / `assert-deterministic` to REFUSE (`:cannot-run`, a named reason) a plan whose world carries slots the artifact cannot represent, instead of silently replaying a different run.

Fence:
- `tools/story/src/re_frame/story/determinism.cljc`;
- `artifact.cljc` (new slot and replay seeding);
- possibly `frames.cljc` (stub registration reuse);
- `tools/story/spec/017-Testing-Story.md` §Run artifact and §Determinism gate;
- tests `determinism_test.cljc` and `golden_test.cljc`.

`promotion.cljc`'s `artifact->variant-body` may want the new seed slot too. No hot-zone file is touched.

## Gates

- JVM: `clojure -M:test` in `tools/story`, where `determinism_test.cljc`, `golden_test.cljc` and `artifact_test.cljc` run.
- `npm run test:cljs`: those suites are `.cljc` and also run in the node lane.

## Decision needed

Yes, one choice. Should `->artifact` (A) fold the variant's whole run-shaping world (decorator stubs, `:db-seed`, frame-setup), so a plan-targeted gate or golden judges the variant's real run? Or should it (B) refuse such a plan with `:cannot-run`, leaving callers to pass an artifact captured from a real run? A is the reading spec 017's "does this plan produce the same run" invites.

